9,15087,429,26553,198,78045,17,87,284,220,18,88,284,481,89,59,60,285,264,1555,382,785,738,315,3501,4930,87,7358,22669,15087,429,26553,198,78045,21,87,284,481,88,284,481,19,89,59,60,285,2441,1555,382,9885,279,9210,1948,1493,5128,11,304,12348,13,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nThe set of points $(x,y,z)$ that satisfy\n\\[2x = 3y = -z\\]is a line.\n\nThe set of points $(x,y,z)$ that satisfy\n\\[6x = -y = -4z\\]is another line.\n\nFind the angle between these lines, in degrees.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"f045b09de53842fd533792ede3e908086bf157ae91bc9b45e66d907607a07bd7"},"seconds":79.56694221496582,"seed":827209390692689098,"stop":"eos","text":"To find the angle between the two lines given by the equations \\(2x = 3y = -z\\) and \\(6x = -y = -4z\\), we first need to express each line in the form of a vector equation. This involves identifying direction vectors for each line.\n\n### Step 1: Identify the direction vector for the first line\nThe equation \\(2x = 3y = -z\\) can be written in parametric form by setting each expression equal to a parameter \\(t\\):\n\\[2x = t \\implies x = \\frac{t}{2},\\]\n\\[3y = t \\implies y = \\frac{t}{3},\\]\n\\[-z = t \\implies z = -t.\\]\nThus, the parametric equations of the first line are:\n\\[x = \\frac{t}{2}, \\quad y = \\frac{t}{3}, \\quad z = -t.\\]\nThis can be written in vector form as:\n\\[\\mathbf{r}_1 = t \\left( \\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{1}{3}, -1 \\right).\\]\nSo, the direction vector of the first line is:\n\\[\\mathbf{d}_1 = \\left( \\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{1}{3}, -1 \\right).\\]\n\n### Step 2: Identify the direction vector for the second line\nThe equation \\(6x = -y = -4z\\) can be written in parametric form by setting each expression equal to a parameter \\(s\\):\n\\[6x = s \\implies x = \\frac{s}{6},\\]\n\\[-y = s \\implies y = -s,\\]\n\\[-4z = s \\implies z = -\\frac{s}{4}.\\]\nThus, the parametric equations of the second line are:\n\\[x = \\frac{s}{6}, \\quad y = -s, \\quad z = -\\frac{s}{4}.\\]\nThis can be written in vector form as:\n\\[\\mathbf{r}_2 = s \\left( \\frac{1}{6}, -1, -\\frac{1}{4} \\right).\\]\nSo, the direction vector of the second line is:\n\\[\\mathbf{d}_2 = \\left( \\frac{1}{6}, -1, -\\frac{1}{4} \\right).\\]\n\n### Step 3: Compute the dot product of the direction vectors\nThe dot product of \\(\\mathbf{d}_1\\) and \\(\\mathbf{d}_2\\) is:\n\\[\\mathbf{d}_1 \\cdot \\mathbf{d}_2 = \\left( \\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{1}{3}, -1 \\right) \\cdot \\left( \\frac{1}{6}, -1, -\\frac{1}{4} \\right) = \\left( \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{6} \\right) + \\left( \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot -1 \\right) + \\left( -1 \\cdot -\\frac{1}{4} \\right) = \\frac{1}{12} - \\frac{1}{3} + \\frac{1}{4}.\\]\nWe need to find a common denominator to simplify this expression:\n\\[\\frac{1}{12} - \\frac{1}{3} + \\frac{1}{4} = \\frac{1}{12} - \\frac{4}{12} + \\frac{3}{12} = \\frac{1 - 4 + 3}{12} = 0.\\]\nSo, \\(\\mathbf{d}_1 \\cdot \\mathbf{d}_2 = 0\\).\n\n### Step 4: Compute the magnitudes of the direction vectors\nThe magnitude of \\(\\mathbf{d}_1\\) is:\n\\[|\\mathbf{d}_1| = \\sqrt{\\left( \\frac{1}{2} \\right)^2 + \\left( \\frac{1}{3} \\right)^2 + (-1)^2} = \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{9} + 1} = \\sqrt{\\frac{9}{36} + \\frac{4}{36} + \\frac{36}{36}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{49}{36}} = \\frac{7}{6}.\\]\nThe magnitude of \\(\\mathbf{d}_2\\) is:\n\\[|\\mathbf{d}_2| = \\sqrt{\\left( \\frac{1}{6} \\right)^2 + (-1)^2 + \\left( -\\frac{1}{4} \\right)^2} = \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{36} + 1 + \\frac{1}{16}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{4}{144} + \\frac{144}{144} + \\frac{9}{144}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{157}{144}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{157}}{12}.\\]\n\n### Step 5: Compute the cosine of the angle between the direction vectors\nThe cosine of the angle \\(\\theta\\) between the two direction vectors is given by:\n\\[\\cos \\theta = \\frac{\\mathbf{d}_1 \\cdot \\mathbf{d}_2}{|\\mathbf{d}_1| |\\mathbf{d}_2|} = \\frac{0}{\\frac{7}{6} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{157}}{12}} = 0.\\]\nThus, \\(\\theta = 90^\\circ\\).\n\nThe angle between the two lines is \\(\\boxed{90}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{90}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
